# M / B006 — manifest checker, repo-root resolver, hook registrations (static analysis; not executed).

C R135 OL ARC-009,ARC-020 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not introduce CQRS handlers, MediatR, Kommand, Vertical Slice Architecture or similar mediator-based organization unless explicitly approved; the manifest check notes MediatR as requiring an approved decision. | backend architecture and NuGet manifests | Explicit approval.
C R136 OL DEP-020 | DEFAULT | When resilience is required the Microsoft resilience packages are approved; direct Polly usage (Polly, Polly.Core) is a documented exception that the manifest check notes. | NuGet manifests | Documented exception.
C R137 OL DEP-004,DEP-010 | MUST NOT | Do not use deprecated or legacy packages without a concrete requirement: the legacy FluentValidation.AspNetCore automatic-validation integration needs a concrete requirement and the deprecated Serilog.Sinks.Elasticsearch sink is flagged. | NuGet manifests | Concrete requirement.
C R138 OL DEP-015 | MUST NOT | NgRx, Axios, Lodash, Bootstrap, Tailwind and additional form, component or state-management libraries are not added by default; an extra library is added only for a concrete need (the manifest check notes them). | npm manifests | Concrete need.
C R139 OL DEP-003 | MUST (manifest check violation) | Pin the latest stable compatible version: missing, floating or range versions in Directory.Packages.props and floating npm specifications are violations; prerelease versions are allowed only when explicitly requested. | NuGet and npm manifests | Prerelease explicitly requested.
C X9 EX DEP-004,DEP-020 | MUST NOT (manifest check violation; no approval path) | Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Polly and Polly.Extensions.Http (deprecated resilience integration packages) must not be added; their presence is reported as a violation with blocking hook feedback. | NuGet manifests | none stated | DEP-004 requires deprecation checks and DEP-020 prefers the Microsoft resilience packages; no oracle policy forbids specific packages outright regardless of approval. | Adding Polly.Extensions.Http produces a blocking manifest violation even when requested.

